# .trivyignore — project-wide reviewed CVE acceptances
#
# This plain, repo-root file is read implicitly by the blocking ghcr publish
# gate and by the GitLab post-build scans. The GitLab pinned-base scan also
# includes these entries when it assembles its effective ignore file.
#
# A base image this repository only pins has a separate, expiring YAML list
# in .trivyignore.base-images.yaml. It is read only by the --pull warning gate.
# The objection to per-gate lists was to a publish-only acceptance that would
# leave development pushes permanently coloured for a finding already ruled
# on. A base-image-only acceptance is the reverse: it reaches only the warning
# gate, whose allow_failure policy already recognises that an upstream rebuild
# is outside this repository's control. It must never silence a built image.
#
# List one CVE ID per line. Every addition needs review: a CVE silenced here
# is a CVE we ship. Prefer upgrading the affected layer or dependency; keep
# the reason beside the ID and reassess on each release.
#
# No project-wide CVEs are currently accepted.
